{"id": "EUVD-2026-103725", "enisaUuid": "b350f6a1-4ce0-32a3-9677-7d5b137563cb", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfilter: ip6t_rt: fix zero-address non-strict match out-of-bounds read\n\nrt_mt6_check() permits rules to be configured with rtinfo->addrnr == 0\neven when address matching (IP6T_RT_FST_MASK) is requested.\n\nIn the IP6T_RT_FST_NSTRICT path, rt_mt6() evaluates packet routing\naddresses against rtinfo->addrs[i] and terminates backwards at the bottom\nof the loop:\n\n    if (ipv6_addr_equal(ap, &rtinfo->addrs[i])) {\n        i++;\n    }\n    if (i == rtinfo->addrnr)\n        break;\n\nWhen addrnr is 0, if the first packet address matches rtinfo->addrs[0],\ni is incremented to 1. Because i is now strictly greater than addrnr (0),\nthe loop termination condition (i == rtinfo->addrnr) is bypassed and will\nnever be satisfied.\n\nIf a crafted IPv6 packet contains matching routing addresses, i will\nadvance past IP6T_RT_HOPS (16). The subsequent call to ipv6_addr_equal()\nreads beyond struct ip6t_rt, triggering UBSAN/KASAN out-of-bounds warnings\nor kernel panics.\n\nFix this by:\n1. Rejecting rules in rt_mt6_check() where IP6T_RT_FST_MASK is set but\n   rtinfo->addrnr is zero.\n2. In rt_mt6(), moving the termination condition (i < rtinfo->addrnr)\n   into the for-loop header condition and removing the backwards break\n   at the end of the loop body.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:16:00", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:20:22", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/959d1829d1ce8b91b435b24a923b51bcc8897090", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fe336bab13834394320997de8b16ca4a913b4f13", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5a54f8b7f7fe207a5c14713015a5820588faf1ad", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b89249819a7d6698bed152feafd3bc6c08489d15", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dd55c0ea87bf70e4e4b3b683acd29ef981335b26", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/191239b0939692e92459d8d32cad14247fa93f89", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d9cf4ac6f326330e1fe4d95671d36a6ff3593f64", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/82313c169eddc02b1bf5ba6b427803e272d3ec42"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98485", "GHSA-mhfj-849g-frgh"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0315a1e2-f515-338d-bb48-f841f02a522f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <b89249819a7d6698bed152feafd3bc6c08489d15"}, {"id": "0f8b37fd-f546-3bc9-ae59-fe732114dee2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <82313c169eddc02b1bf5ba6b427803e272d3ec42"}, {"id": "17dfbb46-07f2-3dcc-b36d-4315ae030cfb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <fe336bab13834394320997de8b16ca4a913b4f13"}, {"id": "1df73ea2-f5a9-3aee-aab7-78423cc5283c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <dd55c0ea87bf70e4e4b3b683acd29ef981335b26"}, {"id": "4b7a6a05-517b-3495-9a01-628bb61055a7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <5a54f8b7f7fe207a5c14713015a5820588faf1ad"}, {"id": "740c99d1-98c9-3dd0-9ffe-4136a63fc14b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "768fecd2-c4e1-3de8-907f-fe61b53096bc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "7c018fd5-dd50-3829-b0d5-c0df67d8f547", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <191239b0939692e92459d8d32cad14247fa93f89"}, {"id": "7dbc809c-8e60-3161-b7c9-74c5f782d50d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.271"}, {"id": "8b83a1ca-8dd4-391d-9d82